+// Cheap per-line prefilters. They exist only for speed and MUST be supersets of
+// the regexes they guard. That is not left to convention: prefilterUnsound is
+// asserted over the whole real tree and over every line each planted mutation
+// changes (see runTests), so a regex alternative added without extending its
+// prefilter fails the suite instead of silently dropping a rule.
+func r1Prefilter(lineLower string) bool {
